    {
      "id": "claim_444b9ff37e5d45af9ce30bedd6042b17",
      "statement": "Providers may optionally support advanced response APIs (e.g., OpenAI Responses API) alongside standard chat completions. These APIs enable streaming tool execution, reasoning outputs, and structured response formats. Implementation requires converting provider-specific response structures (content blocks with type/id/metadata) back to unified AIMessage format via provider-specific conversion functions (e.g., _convert_from_v1_to_responses). Responses API support is optional, configurable via provider-specific parameters (use_responses_api=True), and tested via dedicated test variants (test_responses_standard.py).",
      "evidence": [
